{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqb0kr66rg9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Decision rule for edge kind: parent still OPEN and must finish first -> blocking; parent already DONE but B truly required it (precondition) -> STILL blocking (resilience + costflow + honesty); B merely informed by A, not a precondition -> context; pure knowledge provider (note) -> context.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T14:20:47.122Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqb0kr66rg9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"suggest_links suggest_kind is only ADVISORY. Its done->context default (daemon.js 940/967) is a heuristic for the common case, NOT a constraint. add_dependency accepts an explicit kind; override the hint for true done-prerequisites.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T14:20:47.122Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqb0kr66rg9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Blocking edge from a DONE parent is auto-satisfied (readiness = all non-context deps done, daemon.js ~1092) so it never deadlocks and has no scheduling downside; it only adds correctness if the parent later reopens.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T14:20:47.122Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqb0kr66rg9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Autowire (cosine) deliberately only creates CONTEXT edges, never blocking (daemon.js ~990 filters suggest_kind !== context). So flipping suggest_links done->blocking would not cause autowire to create blocking edges, but it WOULD mislabel merely-related done tasks as prerequisites since the recommender cannot infer precondition-ness — which is why the fix stays behavioral, not in the heuristic.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T14:20:47.122Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb0kr66rg9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Wire true dependencies as blocking edges even when the parent is done","summary":"Edge kind should record STRUCTURAL TRUTH (does B require A?), not execution state. Wire a real prerequisite as a blocking edge regardless of whether the parent is already done; reserve context edges for merely-informative associations that are not preconditions. CORRECTION to an earlier belief: blocking edges do NOT lose Tier-1 context. The get_dependency_summaries / GET /task/context handler (routes/task.js ~line 60) already includes BOTH deps and context_deps summaries (blocking deps come back with via:blocking), so for a done parent blocking vs context is nearly functionally equivalent (readiness auto-satisfied either way, context included either way, frontier weight actually HIGHER for blocking: 1.0 vs 0.5). The note-only auto-inject that injects context_deps only is the separate Tier-2 /search retriever (routes/graph.js DAG tier), not the dependency-context path. Three real reasons blocking is still the correct encoding for a true dependency: (1) RESILIENCE — if the parent reopens (done to in_progress on revert/rework) a blocking edge re-gates the child, a context edge silently will not; (2) COST-FLOW attribution weights blocking 1.0 vs context 0.5 (lib/costflow.js); (3) topological honesty for humans and analytics. ROOT CAUSE of the wrong default: suggest_links hard-codes suggest_kind = (kind==note || status==done) ? context : blocking at daemon.js lines 940 and 967, so the recommender teaches every agent done to context. That hint is ADVISORY — add_dependency takes kind explicitly — so the fix is behavioral: override the suggest_kind hint and wire blocking when the relationship is a genuine precondition. No retrieval-code change is warranted (Tier-1 already carries blocking context); changing the suggest_links heuristic is risky because it cannot infer prerequisite-vs-related and it feeds the autowire safety filter (autowire only ever creates context edges, daemon.js ~990).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T14:20:47.118Z","vec":[-0.1292373687028885,0.03630946949124336,0.039245352149009705,0.003989426419138908,0.06467162072658539,-0.018406450748443604,-0.00044950496521778405,-0.04518523067235947,-0.007163418456912041,0.003868846222758293,0.08168593049049377,0.03582238405942917,-0.050846394151449203,0.012773110531270504,-0.03702211752533913,0.050062406808137894,0.05996505171060562,-0.014060650952160358,-0.013389142230153084,-0.06689955294132233,0.009832283481955528,-0.06615033745765686,0.022993681952357292,-0.0198193471878767,0.024890966713428497,0.06870793551206589,-0.008783222176134586,-0.018155576661229134,0.049042217433452606,-0.05263559892773628,-0.001191000104881823,0.042303815484046936,-0.0846543088555336,0.005198308732360601,-0.0326000340282917,0.02732343226671219,-0.04152408614754677,0.04076354578137398,0.012335370294749737,0.03907117247581482,0.03735823556780815,0.13034294545650482,0.03355458378791809,-0.047932930290699005,-0.023802269250154495,-0.06281012296676636,-0.004928056616336107,0.018335208296775818,-0.0512625016272068,-0.03873758018016815,-0.0001324818003922701,0.0373290590941906,0.0028079512994736433,0.03527738153934479,0.14023873209953308,0.053593069314956665,0.04168183356523514,0.023197274655103683,-0.045024972409009933,0.06661384552717209,-0.026375554502010345,-0.011237083934247494,-0.05177730321884155,-0.056319769471883774,0.00246768188662827,0.10493167489767075,0.02751203253865242,0.005495257209986448,-0.01882772333920002,0.040982138365507126,0.06002054363489151,0.04873424023389816,-0.04612913727760315,0.02741391584277153,0.06315024942159653,0.08968892693519592,0.054002583026885986,0.06984876096248627,0.0005815401673316956,-0.12017054855823517,-0.10620956867933273,0.029605260118842125,0.014821379445493221,-0.016790620982646942,0.010256129316985607,-0.04789130017161369,0.027192186564207077,-0.14035265147686005,0